  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0249' contains five tables: 'user', 'tourist_attraction', 'carousel', 'comment', and 'city_honor'.\nThe 'user' table represents a collection of users. It has five columns: 'creation_time' of type DATETIME, 'email' of type VARCHAR(255), 'password' of type VARCHAR(255), 'user_id' of type INTEGER as the primary key, and 'username' of type VARCHAR(255).\nThe 'tourist_attraction' table represents a collection of tourist attractions. It has six columns: 'attraction_id' of type INTEGER as the primary key, 'attraction_name' of type VARCHAR(255), 'category' of type VARCHAR(255), 'creation_time' of type DATETIME, 'description' of type VARCHAR(255), 'image_url' of type VARCHAR(255), and 'location' of type VARCHAR(255).\nThe 'carousel' table represents a collection of images for a carousel. It has three columns: 'carousel_id' of type INTEGER as the primary key, 'creation_time' of type DATETIME, and 'image_url' of type VARCHAR(255).\nThe 'comment' table represents a collection of comments made by users. It has four columns: 'comment_content' of type VARCHAR(255), 'comment_id' of type INTEGER as the primary key, 'creation_time' of type DATETIME, and 'user_id' of type INTEGER. The 'user_id' column is a foreign key referencing the 'user' table.\nFinally, the 'city_honor' table represents a collection of city honors for tourist attractions. It has five columns: 'attraction_id' of type INTEGER, 'creation_time' of type DATETIME, 'honor_description' of type VARCHAR(255), 'honor_id' of type INTEGER as the primary key, and 'honor_title' of type VARCHAR(255). The 'attraction_id' column is a foreign key referencing the 'tourist_attraction' table. This schema ensures data integrity by enforcing primary key and foreign key constraints, and by maintaining referential integrity by ensuring that the 'user_id' in the 'comment' table corresponds to a valid 'user_id' in the 'user' table, and the 'attraction_id' in the 'city_honor' table corresponds to a valid 'attraction_id' in the 'tourist_attraction' table.",
  "gold_question": "A website provides travel information and user comment functionality. Users can register accounts, leaving details such as username, password, email, and other information. Users can post comments that include the content of the message and the time of posting. The website displays various tourist attractions, including the name, description, location, image URL, and category of each attraction. Each tourist attraction may receive some honors, which include a title and description. Additionally, the website features a carousel functionality that displays some images. The details of the images include the image ID, image URL, and creation time.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0249.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0249\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tourist_attraction` (\n  `attraction_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `attraction_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `image_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`attraction_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `carousel` (\n  `carousel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `image_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`carousel_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `comment` (\n  `comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment_content` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `city_honor` (\n  `honor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `attraction_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `honor_description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `honor_title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`honor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `city_honor_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`attraction_id`) REFERENCES `tourist_attraction` (`attraction_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
